be newly subject to recordkeeping and reporting obligations under the Controlled Substances Act."}],"plainSummary":"This bill expands federal regulation of pill-making machines and their parts. It would require anyone who sells or delivers these machines—not just manufacturers and importers—to keep records and report transactions. The bill also mandates permanent serial numbers on the machines and their critical parts (like dies and punches), and makes it a crime to remove those serial numbers or to handle machines whose serial numbers have been tampered with.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People caught up in the criminal law, and victims of crime.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"C001120","score":0.010894327351796946},"overlapCount":14},"meaning":{"percentile":10.75879476258085,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[{"kind":"sponsor","text":"They wrote this bill. Sponsoring a bill about your own district's industry is the ordinary case, not the odd one."}],"unattributedShare":0.7846913435605308}},{"billId":"119-hr-7651","bioguideId":"H001096","cycle":2026,"score":0.00182681445758012,"matches":[{"industry":"legal","donorAmount":1500,"donorShare":0.00182681445758012,"billConfidence":0.55,"contribution":0.00182681445758012}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"keyword-fallback","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.7846913435605308},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-7651","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"7651","title":"Chloe Cole Act of 2026","introducedDate":"2026-02-23","latestActionDate":"2026-07-15","latestActionText":"Ordered to be Reported (Amended) by the Yeas and Nays: 15 - 8.","policyArea":"Law","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"O000177","cosponsorCount":88,"committeeNames":[